Z||000000||conductor||12-30-2001||07:49 PM||||Hi, its freezing up here and I had to undo my window from ice.<BR>No problem, but there was ice on the window inside the car too!<BR>Is this normal? I only drive short distances lately (sorrry)and the a/c is disconnected(no pump but the buttons on the dash work)<BR>I had this a few times now and I wonder if this is normal or should I search for a leak somewhere?<BR>Grtx Richard.<P>BTW nice signature RO!! Love it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||12-30-2001||07:59 PM||||I would say this is normal for a car with wet/damp interior. It could be wet from from days of rain/snow melting off your boots adn clothes.  I would raise up your floor carpet and feel under it (just the section easyest to get at). If it is wet under the carpet (ie dripping) than I would look for a leak.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mgbringo||12-30-2001||09:29 PM||||Up here in the cold country I try to leave my windows open a little over night once a week or so.  It helps get the moisture out and then the windows fog/ice up less.  <P>Mine sits in the garage so that is easy to do.  If it sits outside you have to make sure it is not snowing, etc.<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||12-31-2001||08:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by conductor:<BR><B>...the a/c is disconnected(no pump ...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh!  Believe the a/c pump is used in the DEFROST position to dehumidify the interior air as welll as defrost the glass.<P>Doesn't seem you are getting anything dried out on the interior. Your body (breath, especially) causes a great deal of moisture to form on the inside and it is never getting dried out.<P>Get your a/c fixed or park indoors with the windows slightly opened over night.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photo.msn.s8.com/MS8zLzAvMS8xMDg3LzE1NS8zMi9INU54UkJyRnlPbnZkaDdvRENhLW13/2a787ccc86b5da461605f26eef23ff8a/clbk=0h9xCkj4Yyo6VbTdcNrmhglJSkAWB6C91volMeDlp0h*oii8TPGa20kyOxpdcqzP8qgFSFmsURSXXLzrLUqyll5ofimdP92*FNFuzBBDM1PEajQxQ*Q8WWq*rfvz6!x4pUtE2EsH24ClDyP3oWXL*C!sOjXA63RMH7rLXNlHSu0Yga0L9A7awE0Vo4vjfHksI0c5clA2zMM!vGsSGqWEfH6rUngsCm7dmRIGCL4B98JxdRCo19jb2zHG1Q2F8!3f0GHxu0h66objRD*CveMNtxaf03Gv9Wi1/jpg.jpg">   <P>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||6
